<title>UK: Lloyds mulls bid for Nationwide - paper.</title>
<headline>Lloyds mulls bid for Nationwide - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lloyds TSB Group Plc is considering launching a takeover bid for Nationwide Building Society if the pro-conversion candidates win considerable backing and force the building society to review its strategy, the Daily Telegraph said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Nationwide, which is now Britain's biggest building society, is scheduled to hold its annual meeting on July 24.</p>
<p>The paper said Lloyds is trying to determine potential synergies of such a move, but that nothing has yet been determined.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
